The public API is the `TaskBatch` class. A new batch is open and empty. `add(payload)` deep-copies and appends any payload while open; after closure it raises `RuntimeError` without copying or storing the payload. `close()` is idempotent, prevents future additions, and must preserve all already queued payloads. `drain()` returns queued payloads in FIFO order and empties the queue; it works both before and after closure. Returned payloads must not alias the original objects passed to `add`, and later mutations of returned payloads must not affect future state. `len(batch)` reports the current queued count, and `batch.closed` is a read-only boolean property.

